        <say>I—I don’t know how I’m going to afford even the most <emph>basic necessities</emph> if I’m just gonna give the guild <emph>everything I make</emph> on this street.</say>

        <say>Not <quote>everything you make</quote>. Just… the extra money you’re able to earn thanks to your privilege. Just what you can spare.</say>

        I stared down at my shoes sullenly. <say>I’m white, so I get paid more than most people here, and I’m less likely to be assaulted. I’m an ex-cop, so the Law is gonna go easy on me, if not <emph>help and protect</emph> me. I have a desirable body and enjoy sex with strangers. I’m blessed with privilege.</say> I sighed. <say>You’re right—I can’t in good conscience keep this. Thank you for pointing this out. Ugh, I hate this…</say> I returned to Gillian. <say>Gillian,</say> I said with a reluctant (if not resentful) sigh, <say>I have decided to donate all of my earnings from tonight.</say>

