        The arguments grew a little louder, and the accusations sharper— <quote>backstabber</quote> and <quote>pig all along</quote> and <quote>probably working undercover the whole time</quote>. I accepted them the way someone in stockades might accept rotten vegetables to the face—with eyes shut tight and a prayer that they would stop any second now. Shosh squeezed my hand, and I focused on that to the exclusion of the voices arguing over which indictment of my character was the most succinct. <say>Don’t listen to them,</say> said both of my best friends in unison.

        Then Yoly emerged from the crowd and, ascending the steps, approached me—followed by Lisa, Paulo, and Ronnie—and reminded me, <say>You promised you would try to avoid roping me into the legal system.</say>

