        <say>I won’t know until I’ve done a few things with a few people, but I expect I will.</say>

        <say>That’s the spirit.</say> I stroked her hair.

        She leaned into my hand and smiled. <say>Would you like to get a head start, Clover?</say>

        <say>I think it might be rude to start the festivities before all my guests—pardon me, all of <emph>our dates</emph> have arrived.</say>

        <say>I suppose.</say> She delicately pulled my hand to her mouth and kissed the backs of my fingers. <say>But that doesn’t mean we can’t <emph>make out.</emph></say>

